    "progressNote": "deliveryRules pass run 2026-09-17 across GA, NJ and MA. 'verified' = a fetched primary source states the rule; 'plan-dependent' = the rule genuinely varies by plan or the published sources conflict; 'unverified' = the field carries a note plus a verifyVia naming the portal, phone line or document that would settle it; 'omitted' = no source and no useful verifyVia. Blocked or unreachable sources this pass: GAMMIS (mmis.georgia.gov) refuses connections, so Georgia's current quarterly ASD manual and live fee schedule could not be read \u2014 the posted January 2018 Part II manual is what Georgia's entries rest on and it predates the 97151-97158 code set. mass.gov returns 403 to automated fetches, so the MassHealth ABA Provider FAQ was not read. The NJ DMAHS ABA newsletter was retrievable only by direct download from web.archive.org. horizonnjhealth.com and aetnabetterhealth.com return HTML stubs or 403 to automated fetches, so no Horizon NJ Health or Aetna Better Health of NJ ABA document could be read."
